-- Hand-written rather than generated by `prisma migrate dev`.
--
-- Liveness beat for in-flight backups, mirroring analysis_job's
-- heartbeat_at. Before this column a `running` row carried no signal
-- separating a live backup from one whose process died (deploy, OOM,
-- host reboot), so everything that needed to know had to guess with a
-- six-hour bound: reclaim waited six hours to be safe, the concurrency
-- guard refused new runs for the same six hours, and the admin page
-- showed "In progress" for a run that was minutes dead, with Delete
-- refusing (409, correctly, for a live run) and Cancel setting a flag
-- nothing would ever poll. Observed live on 2026-08-19: the 02:00
-- scheduled run was killed by the 02:07 deploy and sat undeletable.
--
-- The owning process stamps this from the same two-second timer that
-- polls cancel_requested_at (one UPDATE by primary key, no extra round
-- trip). Reclaim thresholds at five minutes and falls back to
-- started_at for rows that predate the column; those cannot belong to
-- a live process, because shipping this change restarted every
-- replica.
--
-- TIMESTAMPTZ, matching cancel_requested_at on this table.
ALTER TABLE "backup_run" ADD COLUMN "heartbeat_at" TIMESTAMPTZ;
